    <DataNode elementId="AT2G43900-MONOMER" textLabel="inositol-polyphosphate 5-phosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O80560" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">5PTase12 has |FRAME: MG+2 Mg&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|-dependent inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase activity against |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate| when its activity is tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; following expression in yeast. In the same assays, it shows no activity against the membrane-based phosphoinositides (|FRAME: CPD-177 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate|, |FRAME: CPD-1108 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-5-PHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-34-BISPH a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4-bisphosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate|, |FRAME: |, |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate| or |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate|), nor does it show any activity with the soluble tetraphosphate inositol |FRAME: CPD-506 D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate| |CITS: [15574849]|. Interestingly, in addition to its type II 5PTase domain, this enzyme also has a WD40 domain that may be involved in protein-protein interactions |CITS: [15574849]|. 5PTase12 transcripts appear to be expressed equally throughout the plant, though the expression level is somewhat lower in mature leaves. 5PTase12 transcript expression levels do not appear to increase in response to stress |CITS: [15574849]|. &lt;i&gt;5ptase12&lt;/i&gt; mutants are slightly less tolerant to salt based on seedling growth assays in the presence of 150 mM NaCl |CITS: [21677096]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G43900-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G43900.2" />
