    <DataNode elementId="AT2G31830-MONOMER" textLabel="phosphatidylinositol/ inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G31830-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">5PTase14 has |FRAME: MG+2 Mg&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|-dependent inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase activity against |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate| with lower levels of activity against |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate| and the soluble |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate| when its activity is tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; following expression in yeast. In the same assays, it shows no activity against several other membrane-based phosphoinositides (|FRAME: CPD-177 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate|, |FRAME: CPD-1108 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-5-PHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-34-BISPH a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4-bisphosphate|, or |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate|), nor does it show any activity with the soluble tetraphosphate inositol |FRAME: CPD-506 D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate| |CITS: [15574849]|. Interestingly, in addition to its type II 5PTase domain, this enzyme also has a WD40 domain which is typically associated with protein-protein interactions. 5PTase14 transcripts appear to be expressed at higher levels in seedlings and inflorescence apices than in other organs. In addition, 5PTase14 transcript expression levels appear to decrease slightly in response to a dark treatment |CITS: [15574849]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G31830-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase (type II)" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33276, RXN-20320, RXN-20329, RXN-T9-772" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G31830.2" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G31830" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15574849" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G34120-MONOMER" textLabel="type I inositol-1,4,5-trisphosphate 5-phosphatase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q84MA2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">When expressed transiently in Arabidopsis leaf tissue or ectopically in transgenic plants, |FRAME: AT1G34120| allowed for the increased hydrolysis of |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE| and |FRAME: CPD-506| substrates. The enzyme did not hydrolyze |FRAME: D-MYO-INOSITOL-1-MONOPHOSPHATE|, |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-BISPHOSPHATE|, or |FRAME: CPD-193| substrates |CITS: [11402208]|. The geneis is up-regulated in response to |FRAME: Abscisic-Acid|, and is likely acting as a signal terminator of abscisic acid signaling |CITS: [12805629]|.</Comment>
